        detail: "Shoppers are invited to join the fun during the market’s annual Tomato Day Celebration on Saturday, July 25, from 8:00 a.m. to 1:00 p.m. at the Historic Train Depot, 650 Maple Street.\nMarket vendors will offer an incredible selection of locally grown tomatoes and specialty varieties in a wide range of shapes, sizes, and flavors. Shoppers will also find fresh fruits and vegetables, meats, baked goods, coffee, flowers, plants, artisan crafts, and other locally produced goods. In addition to more than 40 local vendors offering fresh seasonal produce and handcrafted goods.\nLive music will be provided by Jacob Dunham, creating the perfect soundtrack for a summer morning at the market.\nThe market will feature several tomato-themed activities throughout the day such as:\nFree Tomato Sammies – Enjoy a complimentary half-sized tomato sandwich while supplies last, made the classic way with fresh Henderson County tomatoes, bread, and Duke’s mayonnaise. Watch and thank our volunteers for assembling these sandwiches fresh throughout the morning.\nTomato Beauty Pageant – Cast your vote for your favorite tomato in the market’s annual Tomato Beauty Pageant, where local growers will showcase some of their biggest, brightest, and most unique tomatoes of the season.\nTerrye Tomato Mascot – Keep an eye out for Terrye Tomato, the market’s cheerful tomato mascot! Terrye Tomato will be strolling around the market, greeting shoppers, posing for photos, and spreading plenty of tomato cheer throughout the morning.",
